#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:10.0]
Everyone wants an AI agent answering on the company Slack. Nobody wants to explain the day it answered wrong. Here's how you get the first -- without risking the second.

[00:10.0 --> 00:29.0]
A humanoid is an agent from a markdown file -- wired to a real channel. Spawn it, register its pane, start its Slack channel, and scope it: it only replies when it's mentioned.

[00:29.0 --> 00:60.5]
Governance: human. Now every reply is a draft. A teammate asks -- and Slack stays silent. The agent does the work; the draft waits in your terminal, clearly marked: not yet posted. A person approves the words before they leave the building. Type send -- and only then, it posts.

[00:60.5 --> 00:64.4]
One reply lands in the thread. The one you approved.

[00:64.4 --> 00:70.0]
When it's earned trust -- flip the switch. Governance: A I. Same agent, now autonomous on that channel.

[00:70.0 --> 00:85.5]
The next question gets answered on its own -- and every exchange still lands in a pane you can read. Autonomy is a dial, not a leap. Slack today -- email and website chat too. rysh dot A I -- we're onboarding design partners now.
